<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 43,991 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 43,991 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 43,991 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday compared to 56,332 tonnes in the same period on Saturday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				     Sunday     October 5</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 2,042	11,229</p>
<p>    Import cargo		41,949	45,103</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and nine berthed. In the next 24 hours, three were expected to sail and 10 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Sugar		    14,000	 Azovlloyed	   6/10</p>
<p>Sugar		    11,913	 Feng Yang	    6/10</p>
<p>Rock phosphate	 30,000	 Justice		7/10</p>
<p>High speed diesel    58,400	 Konpolis	     8/10</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     25,200	 Merkur		 8/10</p>
<p>Iron scrap	     24,839	 Zeyneeb		8/10</p>
<p>Furance oil	    42,000	 Probe Hawk	  11/10</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
